SWEET WLAN run F3 (patch 0136), boot-arg sweetwlan=10 = level 8 (unchanged) + the window 0 dumps of patch 0135 made WHILE THE CA7 RUNS, before the re-halt.
Why: on hardware (run F2, wlan-runF2-0135, observed) RAM at 0x200000 reads all ones once the CA7 is back in reset; the firmware pointers (console, ring_info, mailbox: 0x3ebcec, 0x3ec9ec, 0x3ecd28) are in window 0. With the firmware running the tail window reads fine.
What: swl_f3() runs in W17 after F1 (after its last flags check), before swl_restore: ONE store, cfg 0x84 := 0 (tuple SWT_WIN2_ZERO_E, ONCE, old must be the tail window, read back; no table, value or class is new; none when W17 already stored it). Then the guard (precondition, cfg 0x84 reads 0, [0x200000] not all ones, printed with image word 0, equality NOT required) and swl_f2_dump() (0135's dumps, split out of swl_f2, same lines and caps, swl_f1_span_ok with window 0). All ones or a window that does not read 0 skip the dumps, the run goes on to the unchanged re-halt/restore and the F1 PCIe core group. The F2 block after the restore is not run at level 10 (its guard stops on all ones). BAR0 window (cfg 0x80) untouched while the CA7 runs.
Glue: level 10 accepted, named "F3"; sw3_wr already allows cfg 0x84 as 0 or the tail window; rev gate (level >= 7) unchanged; the glue now also refuses every BAR2 store after the CA7 release (rel bit 4, review 0136 F1). HW-WRITE path: unreviewed.

